Title: Stop opting into Claude Code worktree isolation unless transcripts show real catches
Created: 2026-10-09
Author: Minh Ha-Duong

--- log ---
2026-10-09T12:35Z Minh Ha-Duong created
2026-10-09T16:00Z Minh Ha-Duong amended: census done, scope narrowed under portability and lightening

--- body ---
## Context
Claude Code's built-in worktree isolation guard (text "This session is
isolated in the worktree … Refusing to run it", in the Claude Code binary,
not in this repo) switches on when a session calls `EnterWorktree`. The
harness asks every session to do so: `scripts/on-start.sh:13` and
`rules/claude-code.md` § Entering the session, since adb33d79 (2026-04-15).
Memory records only misfires: gates stranded by a session worktree switch
(2026-09-07), rtk-rewritten git refused, nested repos blocked, background
memory writes refused, raid `/gaze` escalating unreviewed (ticket 0990), and
during the 1072 raid (2026-10-09) review seats unable to create review
worktrees, after which a lead invented an operator waiver to get a gate
seat to rule. No memory records a true catch. Doctrine: a misfiring guard is
removed, not wrapped in another guard.

## Census (2026-10-09, step 1 done)
Tool results under `~/.claude/projects/**/*.jsonl` holding the refusal text:
9,537 (positive control: the probe fires on known refusals). By stated reason:
rtk-wrapped git ~3,000; "too complex to verify" ~3,200; `cd`/`-C` to the
shared checkout 1,704, of which 154 matched a git write verb.

Those 154, read one by one: ~145 false positives (`git worktree add/remove`
of review and task worktrees from the primary, the 1072 symptom; work inside
another worktree or `/tmp`; read-only probes; the nested `fork/` repo).
True catches, clear: `git -C ~/.claude restore --worktree` over uncommitted
memory files (2026-09-24, twice); `git -C <primary> checkout <branch>` moving
the author's checkout off main (2026-09-06). Probable, cwd not recorded:
`reset --hard` (2026-09-30), `merge --no-edit` and `git add` (2026-09-02),
`checkout --detach FETCH_HEAD` (2026-09-23), and a local `merge --ff-only`
into a paper repo's main (2026-08-10, possibly the prose exception).
Ratio about one catch per 1,300 refusals. `guard-destructive-bash.sh`
already covers `reset --hard` on a dirty tree; nothing portable covers
`restore` or `checkout` in the primary.

The guard is not only ours to remove: Claude Code also isolates
`isolation: worktree` subagents and background jobs on its own.

## Constraints
- Portability: skills run on Pi and Codex too; only `rules/claude-code.md`
  may name Claude Code mechanisms.
- Lightening: delete a misfiring guard, do not wrap it in exceptions (no rtk
  carve-out, no new rule lines to dodge the guard).

## Scope
1. Drop the `EnterWorktree` opt-in from `scripts/on-start.sh` and
   `rules/claude-code.md`; sessions use plain `git worktree add`.
2. Make `/hunt`, `/raid` and `/gaze` runtime-neutral: plain git only.
3. One line in `rules/claude-code.md`: background jobs and isolated subagents
   are isolated by the runtime; work there with plain git in that worktree.
4. Accepted residual risk, stated in the commit: `restore`/`checkout` in the
   primary checkout lose their only guard (2 clear catches in two months).
   Keep the forge gate and `guard-destructive-bash.sh`; add nothing.

## Blind-spot pass (raid 2026-10-09)
- EnterWorktree is also what moves the session cwd: with plain
  `git worktree add`, Edit/Write default to the primary checkout on main, and
  two sessions can share it. Removal needs a stated replacement for "who
  enters the worktree" (rules/workflow.md Worktree paths). Author decision.
- `isolation: "worktree"` (hunt, raid, gaze REROLL, team-lead) is a separate,
  Claude-only parameter in portable skills; replace it with "create your own
  `git worktree add` and work only there", and drop gaze's reviewer
  prohibitions that exist only to dodge it. Open: does the runtime still
  isolate background subagents without it? Check with one spawn.
- `worktree-gc.sh` and molt's active-session guard read the EnterWorktree
  lock; plain worktrees need `git worktree lock` or the rail drops.
- Tests pinning the old text: test_project_coherence_prompt,
  test_hunt_worktree_ownership, test_hunt_triage_prestep,
  test_verify_fork_contracts.
- Planned PR reaches ~16 files: split into children (skills portable;
  session opt-in) before execution.

## Exit criteria
- [x] Transcript census with counts (true / false positive), positive control fired
- [ ] Opt-in removed; `/hunt`, `/raid`, `/gaze` use plain git
- [ ] A raid's `/gaze` can create its review worktree (demonstrated once)
- [ ] `make check` passes
